  "name": null,
  "problem": "| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $\\frac{1}{10}$ | $\\frac{1}{5}$ |\n| $X=3$ | $\\frac{1}{5}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ |\n| $X=9$ | $\\frac{3}{20}$ | $\\frac{1}{10}$ |\n\nSuppose $X$ and $Y$ are discrete random variables. Find $\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=0]$ given that the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above and the corresponding conditional expected value is ${\\mu }_{X|0}=\\frac{13}{3}.$",
